This code initializes the pigpio library, opens two I2C handles for the microphones, and sets up signal handlers for graceful shutdown. It reads the raw data from each microphone, converts it to sound pressure level in dB, and logs the timestamped values to `audio_log.txt`. If a read fails, it logs an error value of -999.0 dB. The program runs in a loop until it receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal, at which point it cleans up and exits.

