This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B uses the pigpio library to interface with an external ADS1115 ADC over I2C to sample the analog output of a Melexis MLX91204 Hall effect current sensor. It continuously samples the sensor at 10Hz, logs the converted current readings to a circular buffer of 100 elements, and triggers a warning LED on GPIO17 if the average current exceeds a threshold of 50.0A. The program includes robust error handling for pigpio initialization, I2C bus reads, and sensor-absent conditions. It handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown, ensuring the LED is turned off and resources are released cleanly on all exit paths.

