This C program reads analog values from two Seeed Studio Grove Moisture Sensors connected to an MCP3008 SPI ADC on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the libgpiod API to control the MCP3008 chip-select line and standard Linux spidev for SPI communication. The program logs timestamped moisture readings to a CSV file named `moisture_log.csv` with a 0-100% moisture scale. It handles errors, ensures clean resource release, and gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

