This C program uses the libgpiod library to access the SPI device on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It reads analog data from a DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0 connected to channel 0 of an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. The program logs the raw 10-bit ADC reading and a calculated moisture percentage to the console every 5 seconds. The moisture percentage is clamped between 0% and 100% based on predefined dry and wet calibration ADC values. The program handles errors gracefully and cleans up resources on program exit via signal handling.

