This C program uses the pigpio library to read voltage values from three MCP3008 ADC channels connected via SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It logs the channel number and voltage to a CSV file named 'analog_log.csv' every 500 ms, with timestamps in ISO 8601 format. The program handles SPI communication errors by retrying the transfer up to three times. On SIGINT (Ctrl+C), it closes the SPI handle, terminates pigpio, and closes the CSV file.

