This C program uses libgpiod for GPIO operations (though it's not used in this specific code) and Linux I2C via i2c-dev for bus communication. It continuously monitors the AIN0 analog input channel of a PCF8591 ADC at I2C address 0x48 on bus /dev/i2c-1, performing a dummy read first and then reading the current sample every 100 ms. The sample value (0-255) is printed to stdout. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl-C) cleanly by closing the I2C file descriptor before exiting.

