This C program uses the pigpio library to read analog values from a YL-83 rain sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It samples the sensor once per second, maps the ADC value to a rainfall intensity level, and logs each reading with a timestamp. The program handles SPI errors by retrying the transfer on the next cycle. It also gracefully shuts down on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by closing the SPI handle and terminating pigpio.

