This C program uses the pigpio library to read ADC values from three MCP3008 channels connected via SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It logs the timestamped voltage values for each channel to a file named 'sensor_data.csv' every 5 seconds. The program handles signal interrupts (SIGINT and SIGTERM) to perform a clean resource release, closing the SPI handle and terminating pigpio on exit. The program runs indefinitely, continuously sampling and logging, until it is interrupted.

