This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up GPIO pins for PWM control, opens the SPI device, and enters a loop to read the ADC value every 10 ms. If the ADC value exceeds the threshold, it maps the value to a PWM duty cycle and logs the event. If the ADC read fails, it logs the error and skips the iteration. The program handles graceful shutdown on SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

