This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor an MQ-135 air quality sensor via an MCP3008 ADC connected over SPI on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the sensor value, converts it to an approximate CO2 ppm value using a linear calibration, and activates a ventilation fan if the estimated CO2 level exceeds 700 ppm. The program logs every reading, sampled once every 5 seconds, to 'air_quality.log' in CSV format. It handles SPI communication errors gracefully by logging and retrying rather than crashing, and validates ADC values against the 0-1023 range. The program shuts down cleanly on SIGINT/SIGTERM by turning off the fan, closing SPI, and releasing pigpio resources.

