This code provides a Theremin-like instrument using a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It reads distance from an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor, maps it to a frequency between 220 Hz and 880 Hz, and controls the volume using a photoresistor read via an MCP3008 ADC over SPI0. The program handles sensor read errors, manages resources cleanly on SIGINT, and saves and loads calibration data to 'theremin_config.txt'.

