This code provides a complete solution for reading analog voltage from an MQ-3 alcohol sensor using an MCP3008 ADC connected via SPI on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It logs the readings with ISO 8601 UTC timestamps and classifies the alcohol level based on the PPM value. The program handles errors robustly, retries failed SPI reads, and gracefully shuts down on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

