This code provides a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W using libgpiod v2 and spidev to sample analog audio from an ADMP401 MEMS microphone via a 10-bit MCP3008 SPI ADC. The program handles SPI open/ioctl failures, GPIO chip/line request failures, file open/write/flush failures, and signals (SIGINT, SIGTERM) for graceful shutdown, releasing the GPIO line request, closing the SPI fd, and closing the log file on all exit paths.

