This C program uses the libgpiod library to control a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B with a KY-038 sound sensor and an alarm LED. The program reads the sound sensor's digital output (DO) pin connected to GPIO17 (BCM numbering) and triggers a simulated alarm LED on GPIO18. It prints the sound level reading (0 or 1) to the console each loop iteration with a 100 ms delay between readings. When sound is detected (DO = LOW), it blinks the LED on GPIO18 for 1 second: ON for 1 s, then OFF. The program handles sensor-absent or bus-error paths gracefully, printing an error and exiting if the chip open fails. It also cleans up all GPIO lines and exits cleanly on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM.

