This C program uses the libgpiod library to control a GPIO line for a water pump and the standard Linux spidev SPI interface to read analog soil moisture data from a MCP3008 ADC. The program logs each reading to "soil_moisture.log" with a timestamp, the moisture percentage, and the pump status (ON/OFF), sampling every 60 seconds continuously. It handles initialization steps, sensor read failures, and graceful shutdown on SIGINT.

