This C program captures an MJPEG video stream from a USB webcam connected at `/dev/video0` on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It configures the video capture for a resolution of 640x480 using the V4L2 API directly. The program uses memory-mapped (MMAP) buffers for frame capture and handles input and output asynchronously with `select()`. It logs the timestamp of each captured frame in microseconds to a file named "frame_log.txt". The program includes robust error handling for every V4L2 ioctl call, every file operation, and every memory mapping, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including a graceful shutdown triggered by `SIGINT`.

