This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W uses a PIR motion sensor (HC-SR501) connected to BCM GPIO17 to trigger the Raspberry Pi Camera Module v2 to capture and save a timestamped JPEG image to `/home/pi/images`. It uses `libgpiod` for GPIO input and invokes the `libcamera-still` CLI utility for image capture. The program logs all events, with timestamps, to `/home/pi/motion_capture.log`. It handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` cleanly by releasing all `libgpiod` resources and closing file descriptors.

