This code initializes the APDS9960 sensor using the pigpio library, reads the RGB color values and proximity data every 100 ms, and logs the data to a CSV file when the proximity exceeds 200. It handles I2C communication errors by re-opening the bus and re-initializing the sensor. The program gracefully shuts down on SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

