This C program uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads data from an E18-D80NK IR sensor connected to GPIO 17 and controls a buzzer on GPIO 18 based on the sensor's state. The program logs every state transition with an ISO 8601 timestamp to 'obstacle_log.txt'. It handles errors robustly, including chip open failure, line request failure, and read/write errors. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, releasing all GPIO lines and closing the chip.

