This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with a TDK Chirp ICU-20201 Ultrasonic Time-of-Flight sensor over I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x69. It continuously reads distance measurements by combining the 16-bit distance value from registers 0x31 (high byte) and 0x32 (low byte), sampling every 100 ms. It logs each reading with an ISO 8601 timestamp to 'distance_log.txt', and triggers a GPIO alert on physical pin 17 (BCM 17) if the distance falls below 10.0 cm. The program handles all I2C read/write errors, checks for sensor absence, and manages log file creation errors. It cleansly releases all resources -- I2C handles, GPIO, and pigpio -- on SIGINT/SIGTERM. The main loop ensures that every sample first checks for a signal-requested shutdown, then performs the I2C read, then writes the log entry, so that no partial or corrupted log line is ever produced even if an error occurs mid-sample.

