This code sets up a smart parking gate using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It initializes the I2C bus, configures the GPIO pins for the VL53L1X sensor and servo motor, and sets up an interrupt callback to handle distance measurements. The gate opens when an object is detected within 50 cm and closes when the distance exceeds 60 cm, applying hysteresis. All gate state changes are logged with timestamps and distances to 'parking_log.txt'. The program handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handlers.

