This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the GPIO pins, and configures the I2C bus. It then enters a loop where it triggers a distance measurement on the rising edge of GPIO24, reads the distance from the VL53L1X sensor, and controls a DC motor based on the distance. The motor control logic drives the motor forward if the distance is below 100 mm, backward if above 300 mm, and stops otherwise. The program handles errors, retries I2C transactions with exponential backoff, and stops the motor and releases resources on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

