This code provides a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ that uses libgpiod for GPIO control and the Linux I2C interface to implement a proximity-based interactive art installation with a single MPR121 capacitive touch sensor. The program monitors the 12 electrodes ELE0-ELE11 by polling the touch status registers every 50 ms, triggers distinct 4-bit LED patterns on GPIO 17, 18, 27, and 22 based on which electrode detects proximity, and logs all proximity events to the console with timestamps. The program handles sensor-absent or bus-error paths gracefully and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths using signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

