This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with a Silicon Labs Si1102 proximity sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x60. It configures GPIO27 to raise an interrupt on a rising edge when proximity exceeds a configurable threshold (default 1000). The program reads the 16-bit proximity value from registers 0x08 (high byte) and 0x09 (low byte). On each interrupt, it reads the proximity value, compares it to the threshold, and logs to 'proximity.log' a timestamp, the proximity value, and a status of 'SAFE' if at or below the threshold or 'ALERT' if above it. The program supports command-line arguments for setting the I2C address and threshold. It handles SIGINT for clean shutdown, closing the I2C handle, closing the log file, and terminating pigpio.

