This C program interfaces with a Silicon Labs Si1175 ambient light and proximity sensor using the standard Linux I2C ioctl interface. It reads the 16-bit visible ambient light value from registers 0x22 (low byte) and 0x23 (high byte) every 5 seconds and logs each reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp to a CSV file named 'proximity_log.csv'. The program handles sensor-absent conditions and bus-error paths without terminating unexpectedly, and cleanly releases the I2C file descriptor and the log file on all exit paths, including those triggered by SIGINT and SIGTERM.

