This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ uses the Linux i2c-dev kernel interface to read differential pressure from a Sensirion SDP800-500Pa sensor at address 0x25. It sends the continuous measurement command 0x362F, waits at least 1 ms, reads the 6-byte response, validates the CRC-8 for both values, converts the raw pressure and temperature to their respective units, logs the data to 'airflow_data.txt', and handles I2C write/read errors and sensor-absent paths gracefully. It also cleans up all resources (file descriptors, log files) on all exit paths, including SIGINT.

