This C program uses the pigpio library to read temperature and humidity from a Sensirion SHT35-DIS-B sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x44. It simulates a greenhouse environment monitor by adding a sinusoidal offset to the actual readings. The program logs data in ISO-8601 UTC format to 'environmental_data.txt' every 5 seconds. It handles robust error handling for pigpio initialisation, I2C open/read/write, and file open. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, closing the I2C handle, flushing and closing the log file, and terminating pigpio cleanly.

