This C program for a Raspberry Pi 5 uses the Linux i2c-dev interface to periodically read pressure values from a Melexis MLX90819 sensor on I2C bus 1 at 7-bit address 0x60. It triggers a measurement, reads the 16-bit raw pressure value from the sensor's pressure registers, converts the raw value to kPa using a linear scaling factor of 0.1, and logs each reading to stdout with a timestamp. It handles I2C communication failures and installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to exit cleanly on Ctrl+C.

