This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor a greenhouse with an Adafruit TMP117 High Precision Temperature Sensor over I2C bus 1 at the default address 0x48. It verifies the sensor's device ID register reads 0x0117, reads the temperature register 0x00 (2 bytes, signed, LSB = 0.0078125 °C) every 60 seconds, and appends each reading as a 4-byte little-endian float to a binary file named greenhouse_temps.dat. It handles I2C communication failures gracefully and ensures clean resource release — the I2C handle, the file stream, and the pigpio library — on all exit paths via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling.

