This C program uses the pigpio library to communicate with a Sensirion SDP810-500Pa sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x25. It sends a continuous-measurement command, waits for the first measurement, reads 9 bytes containing pressure, temperature, and status, validates the CRC, converts the raw values, logs the timestamp, differential pressure, and temperature to a CSV file, and handles signals for clean shutdown.

