This C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W uses the Linux I2C ioctl interface to read temperature from a Sensirion STS40 sensor at address 0x44 on /dev/i2c-1. It logs each reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp to temperature_log.txt every 5 seconds in an infinite loop. The program handles errors such as open, ioctl, write, read, CRC mismatch, and file open with descriptive stderr messages and continues looping rather than exiting. It also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler for clean shutdown that closes the file descriptor and the log file.

