This C program uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi Zero W's GPIO and I2C bus. It reads the ambient and object temperatures from the MLX90614ESF-BAA sensor, converts them to Celsius, and logs them to a file with timestamps. The program also controls a cooling fan on GPIO 18 based on the object temperature, using hysteresis to prevent rapid switching. The program handles errors, retries failed I2C operations, and cleans up resources on exit.

