This C program uses the pigpio library to communicate with a Sensirion SDP800-500Pa sensor over the I2C bus. It initializes the pigpio library, opens the I2C bus, and sets up a signal handler for graceful shutdown. The program continuously sends a measurement command to the sensor, waits for the measurement to complete, reads the 6 bytes of data, and calculates the CRC-8 checksums for both the pressure and temperature data. If the CRC checks pass, it logs the raw 16-bit pressure and temperature values to the console. The program handles errors during initialization, I2C operations, and CRC checks, and ensures that resources are properly released on exit.

