This C program uses the pigpio library to control a PWM-driven cooling fan on GPIO18 (BCM) based on the CPU temperature read from `/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp`. It adjusts the fan speed linearly between 0% and 100% duty cycle as the temperature changes between 40°C and 70°C. The program logs the timestamp, temperature, and duty cycle to `fan_log.txt` every 5 seconds. It handles file write errors, temperature read failures, and pigpio initialization failures gracefully. The program cleans up all resources on SIGINT/SIGTERM — stops the fan, closes files, and terminates pigpio.

