This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B monitors a BMP180 sensor over I2C at address 0x77 on `/dev/i2c-1`, sampling once per second and logging timestamped temperature/pressure breaches outside predefined thresholds to `breach_log.txt`. It uses the Linux I2C dev interface, integer arithmetic for BMP180 calibration calculations, and handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths. It also includes clean resource release on all exit paths with signal handling for `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`.

