This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to sample a BMP180 pressure/temperature sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x77 every 500 ms using a pigpio hardware timer callback. It stores timestamped readings in a 60-entry circular buffer and drives a cooling fan on GPIO18 (active-high) when the temperature exceeds 30°C. The program handles SIGINT/SIGTERM by turning the fan off, closing the I2C handle, and calling gpioTerminate. It prints each new reading to stdout and keeps the timer callback simple, avoiding blocking calls such as printf or I2C functions inside it where possible.

