This C program uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and I2C interfaces. It toggles data logging from a BMP180 pressure sensor at I2C address 0x77 to a file named `pressure_log.txt`. The toggle is driven by falling-edge detection on GPIO27, debounced with a 200 ms window. The program reads the BMP180's calibration data and uses it with the Bosch compensation formulas to compute pressure from the raw sensor bytes, writing a new log line every 2 seconds for as long as logging remains enabled. It handles I2C communication errors, pigpio library initialization failures, and cleans up all open resources on receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

