This C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B uses the pigpio library to toggle data logging from a BMP180 pressure sensor to `pressure_log.txt` via a push-button interrupt on GPIO4. The program reads the BMP180 calibration coefficients from registers 0xAA-0xBE at startup and validates them. It uses oversampling OSS=3 for pressure measurements with the correct 26 ms conversion delay and implements the full Bosch BMP180 compensation algorithm using integer arithmetic. The program logs only when logging is enabled; when disabled, it prints a status message. It samples every 2 seconds and handles SIGINT cleanly by closing the I2C handle and releasing pigpio resources before exiting.

