This C program interfaces with an Analog Devices ADPD144RI sensor over I2C on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using libgpiod for GPIO control and the Linux I2C character-device interface. It reads the 16-bit red and IR channel data from the FIFO data register, triggers an LED if the IR reading exceeds a threshold, and logs timestamped readings to a CSV file. The program handles I2C read/write errors, sensor-absent conditions, and graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

