This C program uses the libgpiod API to sample the analog audio output of an Adafruit MAX9814 Electret Microphone Amplifier. It configures GPIO 17 as an input and GPIO 18 as an output, setting the output to LOW to select 60dB gain. The program polls the digital input pin at a 10 ms interval, detecting rising edges to identify peak sound events. Each detected peak is logged to `audio_log.txt` with a timestamp and a level of 1. The program handles all libgpiod initialization and I/O errors robustly, checking the return value of every API call. It ensures clean release of all libgpiod resources on all exit paths via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling. The program runs indefinitely until interrupted.

