This C program uses the libgpiod v1 API to monitor a SainSmart TTP223B capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO 17 on a Raspberry Pi 5. It opens the gpiochip0 by name, requests the line as input with the consumer label "ttp223_tamper", and polls the line every 100 ms using CLOCK_MONOTONIC. If the sensor remains continuously touched for more than 5 seconds, it prints an intrusion alert to stdout once per touch event. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, releasing the line and closing the chip on all exit paths.

