This C program uses the pigpio library to read RPM from a Melexis MLX90217 Hall-effect sensor connected to GPIO 4 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It counts rising-edge pulses in a 1-second window, computes RPM, and logs the result to 'rpm_log.txt' and prints it to stdout. The program handles errors, installs signal handlers for clean termination, and releases resources on exit.

