This C program interfaces with a SainSmart TTP223B digital capacitive touch sensor and an LED on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the libgpiod library. It polls the touch sensor every 50 ms, illuminates the LED only while the sensor is actively touched, and logs all touch events, errors, and startup/shutdown messages to the system syslog. The program handles graceful shutdown via SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handlers to ensure the LED is turned off and resources are released before exiting.

