This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor a liquid flow sensor on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It initializes the I2C bus, sends a command to start continuous measurement, reads the sensor data, validates the CRC, converts the raw flow value to ml/min, and logs the results to a CSV file. The program handles errors, retries on I2C failures, and gracefully shuts down on SIGINT.

