This C program uses the libgpiod library to read digital reflectance data from two TCRT5000 IR obstacle-avoidance sensor modules on GPIO17 and GPIO27, each active-low. It drives an LED on GPIO22 high when both sensors read 0. The program polls the sensors every 100 ms and logs each sample to a comma-separated file 'obstacle_log.csv' with columns timestamp, sensor1, sensor2, led_state, flushing after each write. It handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for graceful shutdown by turning off the LED, releasing all line resources, closing the chip, and closing the log file.

