This C program reads acceleration data from a GY-45 MMA8451Q accelerometer over the I2C bus 1 at address 0x1D. It uses the Linux i2c-dev ioctl interface for I2C access and libgpiod for the LED GPIO line on GPIO17 (BCM numbering). The program verifies the sensor's identity by reading the WHO_AM_I register and checking it equals 0x1A before operation. It polls the sensor every 100 ms and triggers the LED if the magnitude of acceleration on any axis exceeds a threshold of 2.0g. When an impact is detected, the LED is turned on for 500 ms, and a timestamped entry is appended to 'impact_log.txt'. The program handles I2C read/write errors gracefully and cleans up all resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

