This C program uses the libgpiod library to read an E18-D80NK IR obstacle sensor connected to GPIO17 on a Raspberry Pi 5. It opens the gpiochip device for GPIO17 on the Raspberry Pi 5 (gpiochip4) and requests the line for input direction. The program polls the sensor every second; when an obstacle is detected (line reads LOW), it triggers a simulated "self-parking" sequence logged to the console with timestamps. The program handles errors, checks all libgpiod calls, and handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for clean shutdown, releasing the GPIO line and closing the chip on all exit paths.

