This C program uses the pigpio library to control two DC motors driven by an L298N controller. It reads simulated ultrasonic distance sensor values for each motor and maps these distances to PWM duty cycles to control the speed of the motors. The motors are driven forward if the distance is below 50 cm and backward if the distance is 50 cm or above. The program runs in a loop every 100 ms and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure proper cleanup.

