This code sets up a smart irrigation system using the libgpiod library on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It controls four 5V relay modules connected to GPIO17, GPIO23, GPIO24, and GPIO25. The program generates a simulated soil-moisture value every 10 seconds and activates the relays if the moisture level is below 30. It logs each activation with a timestamp, relay number, and moisture level to `irrigation_log.txt`. The program handles signals to deactivate the relays and clean up resources before exiting.

