This C program initializes the MPU-6050 gyroscope on the Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the Linux i2c-dev ioctl interface. It wakes the sensor from sleep, sets the gyroscope full-scale range to ±250 dps, and continuously reads the 6 bytes of gyroscope data starting at register 0x43. The raw signed 16-bit big-endian values are converted to degrees/second using the 131.0 LSB/dps sensitivity factor, and the x, y, and z axis readings are logged to the console. The program handles sensor-absent or bus-error paths gracefully and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths using SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling.

