```

This C program for a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ reads angular velocity from an InvenSense MPU-6050 gyroscope over SPI using the Linux spidev interface with libgpiod for manual chip-select control on GPIO8 (CE0). It configures SPI at approximately 3.9 MHz, mode 0, and asserts the CE0 chip-select line via libgpiod for each transfer. The program reads gyroscope X, Y, and Z axis data from registers 0x43, 0x45, and 0x47 (high bytes) with auto-increment disabled, using single-byte reads, and converts the raw 16-bit two's-complement values to degrees per second using the 131.0 LSB/(deg/s) sensitivity factor. It stores each reading, with its timestamp, in a 64-entry in-memory circular buffer. If any axis exceeds ±200 deg/s, it blinks an LED on GPIO17 (physical pin 11) with 500 ms on/off intervals. The program handles SPI initialisation failures and sensor read failures, and on SIGINT (Ctrl+C), it prints the entire circular buffer as CSV with columns Timestamp, X, Y, Z, then releases the SPI handle and GPIO resources on every exit path.

