This C program uses the pigpio library to detect seismic activity with two Omron D7E-2 tilt sensors on BCM GPIO23 and GPIO24. It registers edge-triggered callbacks for both rising and falling edges on each sensor. When both sensors simultaneously read HIGH for a continuous duration of at least 500 milliseconds, it triggers an alert by setting GPIO17 HIGH for 2 seconds, then LOW. It logs each seismic event to `seismic_events.txt` with an ISO-8601-style timestamp. The program handles errors during pigpio initialization, log file opening, and callback registration. It also includes signal handlers to close the log file, set the alert pin LOW, and terminate pigpio when interrupted.

