This code initializes the TCS34725 color sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x29 using the pigpio library. It sets the sensor to power on and enables RGBC measurement, and configures the integration time to 154 ms. The program reads the clear, red, green, and blue values every 500 ms and logs them to a CSV file named `color_data.csv`, including a Unix-epoch timestamp. It handles errors during I2C operations by setting the sensor values to 0 for that cycle and continues running. The program also includes signal handlers to clean up resources when interrupted by SIGINT or SIGTERM.

