This C program uses the pigpio library to control four SainSmart 5V relay modules on BCM GPIO pins 4, 17, 27, and 22. It simulates a smart greenhouse irrigation system by reading random moisture sensor values and controlling the relays accordingly. The program logs each sensor reading, relay state, and timestamp to `irrigation_log.txt`. It handles errors during initialization, log file opening, and GPIO operations, and safely deactivates all relays and closes the log file on SIGINT or any error.

