This C program uses the pigpio library to read acceleration data from an Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer over I2C bus 1 at address 0x18. It initializes pigpio and I2C with error checking, configures the LIS3DH for a 100 Hz data rate and ±2g full scale, and continuously reads 16-bit signed acceleration values starting from register OUT_X_L (0x28). It converts the acceleration values to g using a sensitivity of 16384 LSB/g and detects freefall when the acceleration magnitude drops below a user-defined threshold (default 0.2g) and impact when it exceeds another user-defined threshold (default 1.5g). On impact, it activates a buzzer on GPIO17 for 1 second. The program handles optional command-line freefall and impact thresholds, retries I2C communication failures, and performs graceful cleanup on SIGINT. It ensures resources are released on every exit path.

