This C program uses the pigpio library to read acceleration data from an Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer over I2C. It configures the sensor for ±2g range, high-resolution mode, and 100 Hz output data rate. The program reads acceleration at 10 Hz, computes g as the 16-bit signed raw value shifted right 4 bits and scaled by 0.0009765625, and logs events exceeding a user-defined threshold to `/var/log/high_acceleration.log`. If the threshold is exceeded, the program triggers a system shutdown. The program handles I2C open/configuration errors, sensor read errors, and graceful exit on SIGINT.

