This C program uses the libgpiod library to monitor a conveyor-belt motor using an A3144 Hall-effect sensor on GPIO 17. It configures the GPIO line as input with an internal pull-up, sets up edge-triggered event detection with a 2 ms debounce window, and computes RPM every 5 seconds. The RPM values are logged to a CSV file with timestamps and printed to stdout. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown and releases all resources before exiting.

