This C program uses the libgpiod library to control two Adafruit Solenoid Valves through relay modules on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It implements a timed water distribution schedule, activates each valve for a specified duration, and logs each event with an ISO 8601 timestamp. The program handles GPIO chip initialization failures, gpiod_line_request_output failures, and file I/O errors. It also ensures clean GPIO release and file closure on exit through signal handling.

