This C program uses the libgpiod library to control two vibration motors connected to a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B through GPIO lines 17 and 27. The program pulses the motors sequentially, with motor 1 for 200 ms and motor 2 for 300 ms, repeating indefinitely. It handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to gracefully stop the motors and release the GPIO lines. Error checking is performed on every gpiod call, and resources are released on all exit paths.

