This C program uses the pigpio library to decode NEC IR remote signals from an IR receiver connected to GPIO17 (BCM). It registers a pigpio alert callback on the falling edge to capture pulse timings, decodes the 32-bit NEC frame, validates the decoded command against its inverted copy, logs the decoded address and command to syslog, and publishes each decoded command as JSON to an MQTT broker at localhost:1883 on topic ir/decoded. The program handles errors, cleans up resources on exit, and gracefully shuts down on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

